WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.500
To celebrate the release of Insurgent, let’s
take a look at 15 things you probably didn’t

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:11.499
know about the big-screen adaptation of Veronica
Roth’s best-selling novel.

00:00:11.499 --> 00:00:17.840
The Amity set was built in Serenbe, a sustainable
community about 30 minutes southwest of Atlanta.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:22.920
Despite bad weather, it took the film’s
crew just six weeks to build the 13-acre Amity

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:23.920
set.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.410
More than 200 people worked seven days a week
to create the Amity Dome with its central

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:34.760
tree, build a crumbling concrete freeway overpass,
and modify the stables at Serenbe.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.160
Dozens of crew also planted vegetables, flowers
and grass crops.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.019
The Amity dome was a large structure made
of wood and glass.

00:00:44.019 --> 00:00:49.579
It measured 65 feet tall and 100 feet around,
and the crew only just managed to complete

00:00:49.579 --> 00:00:53.339
it on the morning it was needed for filming.

00:00:53.339 --> 00:00:59.039
Prosthetics make-up artist Margie Ka-klamanos
was employed especially to create Amity leader

00:00:59.039 --> 00:01:01.170
Johanna’s signature facial scar.

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:06.460
Actress Octavia Spencer said that having the
scar applied really helped put her in Johanna’s

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:07.460
world.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:13.130
According to Octavia Spencer, actor Ray Stevenson,
who plays Four’s father Marcus, would sometimes

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.650
sing to her before they started filming.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:21.939
Although Tris does cut her hair in the Insurgent
novel, it isn’t as short as Shailene Woodley’s

00:01:21.939 --> 00:01:22.939
in the movie.

00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:27.820
Between filming Divergent and Insurgent, Woodley
cut her hair very short for her role in the

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.549
movie The Fault In Our Stars.

00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:35.039
And she decided to keep it that way for Insurgent
as she didn’t want to wear a wig.

00:01:35.039 --> 00:01:39.049
The movie’s stunt team was impressed with
the athletic ability of actor Jai Courtney,

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:40.939
who plays Dauntless leader Eric.

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:45.680
According to the movie’s stunt co-ordinator,
they even had to ask Courtney to slow down

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:50.140
as he was running too fast for the cameramen
filming him!

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:55.100
The military vehicles that transport Dauntless
leaders Max and Eric to the Amity faction

00:01:55.100 --> 00:02:00.960
weighed 55,000 pounds and were decommissioned
troop carriers from Afghanistan.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:06.979
Director Robert Schwentke wanted authenticity
when it came to the weapons used in Insurgent.

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:12.230
In other words, he wanted the guns to actually
fire and for us to see the recoil, the flash

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:13.950
and the shells being discharged.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:19.110
So, the movie’s art department based their
designs on existing firearms, and made casings

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.640
that fit onto real weapons.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.220
The Factionless set was four stories high
and filled a whole warehouse and even some

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.340
of its parking lot!

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:31.430
The set was retro and steampunk in style.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:36.260
As Factionless leader Evelyn, actress Naomi
Watts wore a jacket that started life as a

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.260
vintage piece.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.930
But the filmmakers wanted to add more contrast
to it, so they threw bleach at the jacket,

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:45.610
creating the look we see in the film.

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:50.970
The large set for Erudite headquarters was
built at Screen Gems Studios in Atlanta.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:55.580
The laboratory was the most complex part to
build because it lacked straight lines as

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.790
its ceiling and walls were all curved.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:04.940
The laboratory set was 10,000-square-foot,
and had bulletproof glass and 16 projectors.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:09.590
The mysterious box which features in Insurgent
doesn’t appear in the original book.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:14.209
The filmmakers wanted the box to have both
an ancient and hi-tech feel to it, and many

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:17.069
different designs were tried out before they
settled on its look.

00:03:17.069 --> 00:03:22.410
The movie’s prop master teamed up with artisans
in Los Angeles to create the box we see in

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.700
the film.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:28.760
In the novel, Chicago’s Merchandise Mart
is home to Candor Headquarters.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:33.110
But, the filmmakers created Candor in Atlanta’s
AmericasMart.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:38.721
The filmmakers closed down part of Peachtree
Street, the main street in Atlanta, so they

00:03:38.721 --> 00:03:43.140
could safely film a complicated attack sequence
at Candor Headquarters.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:47.480
The scene involved stuntmen abseiling off
buildings as well as firing weapons while

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:52.450
zip-lining from nearby rooftops to the rooftop
of the AmericasMart building.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:58.620
Although Insurgent was mainly shot in Atlanta,
the production also filmed briefly in Chicago.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:03.550
The Chicago shoot involved opening all the
bridges at once over the Chicago River and

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.659
stopping all its boat traffic.

00:04:05.659 --> 00:04:09.560
Well there you have it, 15 things you probably
didn't know about Insurgent!

